design/mfg/specs/band-flex-tails.md:46:Length, width and path of each tail are open point 4: the architecture gives none. The 3D model (design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md, model v6.2) uses width 1.4 (X -3.3 to -1.9) and the floor slot 2.0 x 0.6 from X -3.5 to -1.5 (before v6.2 2.6 x 0.6 at X -3.5 to -0.9) at Y = +-5.9, with the bottom at Z -0.20 (US 7 and 8), -0.23, -0.63, -1.04, -1.45 and -1.85 (US 9 to 13) (17.26); a free volume 2.6 x 2.2 x 1.03 beside each slot under the board holds one fold (model v5 figure: X -3.5 to -0.9, Y +-3.4 to +-5.6, Z 0.40 to 1.43; not measured again for the shorter slot). Whether one fold of the 0.15 ribbon fits that height (bend radius) is the flex maker's (open point 4).
design/mfg/specs/v5-refresh-notes.md:3:Files: body.md, joystick-nub.md, main-board.md, cover-glass.md, band-flex-tails.md (all in design/mfg/specs/). Line numbers are the lines in the files as they stand now. Sources: TN = design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md (section Model v5, lines 99 to 200); AR = design/architecture.md section number (17.11, 17.15, 17.19, 17.21, 17.22, 17.23, 17.24); MP = design/mech/mic-path/mic-path.md; LP = design/mech/light-path/light-path.md; AS = design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md. No number was invented. Per-size values (motor angle, protection circuit start, floor slot depth) are written at US 9 with one sentence that the per-size value follows from the next model version (AR 17.24). Flange 6.9 and the 6.4 x 6.4 stiffener are written as "to follow" (AR 17.24 rulings K12, K13).
