design/mfg/specs/body.md:3:Design version A5, architecture section 17.8 (2026-11-10), refreshed to the inside model v6.2 (architecture 17.11, 17.15, 17.19, 17.21, 17.24 to 17.27; exterior merged32f, and merged32g on US 7 and US 8). All dimensions in mm. Axes: X along the finger (+X fingertip), Y across (-Y is the joystick side, the side the thumb works; the older name "+Y thumb side" is retired, 17.11), Z up. Angles are measured around the finger from the top of the band; minus is the joystick side (the joystick is at -78 degrees on US 9 to 13, motor at -44 degrees on US 9; the values per ring size are in the last section).
design/mfg/specs/body.md:8:The one-piece metal body of the ring: a flat block (holds screen, board, glass) that flows through two shoulders into an 8.0 mm wide band that goes round the finger. The band is a hollow channel, open toward the finger, later closed by the band liner (specs/band-liner.md). It carries the pockets and openings for the screen, glass, 2 microphone floor pockets with their holes and seats on the underside, 2 floor slots, the joystick opening and pocket, and the motor pocket. The ring has one control, the joystick (17.11): no record button, no record cap and no opening for one. The four charging pads sit in the liner on the inside of the band, so the body has no pad holes (17.12). Before v5 this page listed microphone wall slots, a record cap opening, 4 pad holes and the joystick at 150 degrees.
design/mfg/specs/body.md:90:Floor slots 2.0 x 0.6 at Y = +-5.9, from X = -3.5 to X = -1.5 (two; model v6.2, architecture 17.27: shortened from 2.6 x 0.6 to keep at least 0.30 mm of metal beside the motor pocket). On ring sizes US 7, 8 and 9 the motor pocket opens into the block's cavity through a window of about 4.0 x 1.1 mm (the pocket grown by 0.30 mm intersected with the cavity grown by 0.30 mm), closed at assembly by the sealant plug SEAL2; on US 10 to 13 a wall of at least 0.30 mm stands there. Motor pocket angle per size: -47.0, -45.5, -44.0, -45.0, -43.5, -42.5, -42.5 degrees on US 7 to 13; the pocket floor lies 0.05 mm under the motor. Earlier text of this line: floor slots 2.6 x 0.6 at X = -2.2 (corrected 2026-11-11 from X = -4.7: inside model, thin-notes.md K7; assembly.md conflict K-A10). The bottom of each slot lies at Z -0.20 on US 7 and 8, then -0.23, -0.63, -1.04, -1.45, -1.85 on US 9 to 13 (17.26, model v6), so each ribbon reaches the band channel at every size. Beside each slot, under the board, 2.6 x 2.2 x 1.03 mm stay free for one ribbon fold (K-A6). Panel pocket = panel + 0.05 per side (27.45 x 12.9), corner radius 0.1. The microphone pockets, holes and seats are in the table above; no microphone slot exists in any wall. These are the modeller's choices; the maker takes the STEP file for the final geometry once the parts helper has delivered it.
design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:6:The thumb control: one rounded rectangular nub in a raised frame, on the joystick side of the band at -78 degrees on US 9 to 13 (78 degrees from the top; -81.0 on US 8 and -84.0 on US 7, 17.25; the ring has no record button, the joystick is the one control). It tilts; under it five switches (SW1 up, SW3 down, SW4 toward the hand, SW5 toward the fingertip, Alps SKTAAAE010, 2.6 x 1.6 x 0.53 each) sit in a cross at 2.4 mm from the centre, and the centre switch SW2 sits between them (17.15). A press on the centre closes SW2; a long press of 1.0 s starts or stops a recording (17.11). The nub with its flange is one moulded part (architecture 17.3). Before v5: four switches in a cross at 2.1 mm at +150 degrees.
design/mfg/specs/cell.md:6:A thin rechargeable cell bent to follow the band: 1.6 mm thick, 6.0 mm wide, 33.936 mm (US 7) to 46.121 mm (US 13) long on its centre line, 39.175 mm at US 9 (centre-line radius 10.5726 mm at US 9; arc 212.301 degrees at US 9, from +48.713 degrees through the bottom to -98.986 degrees). Start and end angle, length and capacity per ring size are in the table "Ring sizes" below (architecture 17.26, measured in the inside model v6). The cell has a 2.0 mm sealed edge and its two tabs at the +Y end. A protection circuit of 1.5 x 5 mm sits on the cell's tab, before the cell's start (at US 9 from +39.5 to +47.6 degrees, 0.2 mm before the cell). A temperature sensor line goes with the cell (one line on FLEX2). Before v5 this page gave 28.4 mm, an arc from -39 to +167 degrees and 15 to 20 mAh (architecture 17.10, replaced by 17.15 and 17.26).
design/mfg/specs/record-cap.md:1:# Specification: record cap reference CAP2 (design/bom.csv line 78, design/mfg/part-map.csv)
design/mfg/specs/record-cap.md:3:This part does not exist. The ring has one control, the joystick (architecture 17.11). The record cap of earlier versions was removed on 2026-11-10. Do not make this part.
